Chapter: DiagGop
  cites Works chapter GopHandoff
  cites Diag chapter DiagStage

 We say:

Section: The Stage

 The mode selection runs in the UEFI stub before ExitBootServices and this
 stage runs after it, so QueryMode and SetMode are both gone by the time
 anything here could ask. The stub therefore banks what it did into the
 handoff block (v3), and this row reports the bank rather than re-deriving it.

 The six states are distinguishable on purpose. Geometry is not: a box that
 paints 1024x768 reads identically whether that was the largest mode the
 firmware offered or whether SetMode was refused and the firmware's own
 console mode is still up. That ambiguity is the whole reason the bank exists,
 and reporting a bare pass or fail here would put it straight back.

  dgop-states : List Text = ["honoured", "kept", "single", "refused", "noloop", "nostub"]

  dgop-state : Integer -> Text
  dgop-state (dummy) =
    if handoff-has-v3 0 == False then "nostub"
    else if handoff-gop-maxmode 0 == 0 then "nostub"
    else if handoff-gop-maxmode 0 == 1 then "single"
    else if handoff-gop-ran 0 == False then "noloop"
    else if handoff-gop-called 0 == False then "kept"
    else if handoff-gop-status 0 == 0 then "honoured"
    else "refused"

 nostub and noloop are the instrument's own failure states and are warnings,
 not verdicts about the box: the first says an older stub booted this image,
 the second says the bank disagrees with itself and nothing here can be
 trusted. refused is the one real negative answer, and it is the answer the
 sitting is for.

  dgop-colour : Text -> Integer
  dgop-colour (st) =
    if st == "refused" then diag-col-bad
    else if st == "noloop" then diag-col-warn
    else if st == "nostub" then diag-col-warn
    else if st == "single" then diag-col-note
    else diag-col-good

  dgop-said : Text -> Text
  dgop-said (st) =
    if st == "honoured" then "firmware moved to the largest mode it enumerated"
    else if st == "kept" then "largest mode was already current, nothing asked"
    else if st == "single" then "firmware enumerated one mode, nothing to choose"
    else if st == "refused" then "SetMode REFUSED the largest mode"
    else if st == "noloop" then "v3 bank present but the loop never ran"
    else "no v3 handoff: this image was built by an older stub"

  dgop-run : DiagCtx -> DiagResult
  dgop-run (c) =
    let st = dgop-state 0
    in let g1 = "max=" & show (handoff-gop-maxmode 0) & " before=" & show (handoff-gop-mode-before 0) & " chose=" & show (handoff-gop-mode-chosen 0) & " flags=" & show (handoff-gop-flags 0) & " status=" & diag-hex8 (handoff-gop-status 0)
    in let g2 = "fb=" & show (c.dc-w) & "x" & show (c.dc-h) & " stride=" & show (c.dc-stride) & " hv=" & show (handoff-version 0) & "  " & dgop-said st
    in diag-result st (dgop-colour st) [g1, g2] [g1, g2]
